Package: organize-dl
Version: 0.1.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Ivanadrian31 <ivanadrian31@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: 24
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: bash (>= 4.2)
Homepage: https://github.com/Ivanadrian31/organize
Description: sort a downloads folder into category subfolders
 organize-dl moves the files of one directory into Images, Documents,
 Music, Videos, Archives and Others subfolders, chosen from the file
 extension.
 .
 Only regular files directly inside the directory are touched; hidden
 files, subdirectories and symlinks are left alone. An existing file is
 never overwritten: a collision becomes name_1.ext, name_2.ext and so
 on. A --dry-run flag prints the plan without moving anything.
